#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128880 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c28b8ae-71ef-5d26-895a-5d949fc5b164" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Components of the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "6bba4758-678a-5bf6-b9df-cdc2662ab306" :question/math-academy-id "e-5525" :question/problem "If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/3e677aa7f2db1cc637e0566a60813ebae1e2bccf80325106317c1d2b7717c2a5.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/67a421166c674275ae14da43962c8e5c8ea37b6a9c8a0548d5b09428b703d831.png) are the real and imaginary parts of the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/fde83769f627e95f5dfe3285bf275ebfe1678710a36c264b6662248063470bb0.png) then what is the value of $ad+eh?$" :question/worked-solution "For the given matrix $A,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2-3\\text{i} & -5-7\\text{i} \\\\ 1-6\\text{i} & 5-9\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(A)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -7 \\\\ -6 & -9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(A)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $a=2,d=5,e=-3$ and $h=-9.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nad+eh=2 \\cdot 5 + (-3) \\cdot (-9) = 37.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128881 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2e7753-83f4-5826-a04f-89616d34c578" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations to a Complex Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "0f32e78f-a13d-5e81-ba64-bff28a61aacf" :question/math-academy-id "e-5526" :question/problem "Given the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/766ddf98a05c69ef0791858a7f32457425cf1a9650d2205227ffc7d9d173d2e7.png) find the result of applying to $A$ the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\nR_1 := \\dfrac{1}{\\textrm{i}}R_1, \\qquad R_2 := R_2 - 2\\textrm{i}R_1\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the row operations to $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} & -\\text{i} \\\\ 2+2\\text{i} & 1\\end{aligned}]\\, &  & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{\\text{i}}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2+2\\text{i} & 1\\end{aligned}]\\, &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2\\text{i}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the result is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/9fef320d53c15c2820719bb1d0dfabb00afa6200b43279e3137fbb25c4e67e2d.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128909 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83fad21d-6b36-5198-a13f-362d34342475" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Complex Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "27f2c303-b9a9-5337-bcea-865a9273b35b" :question/math-academy-id "e-5902" :question/problem "If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/b696bb055794a4ff94c86abc39ef3929113f82683b548a933fc1103245eff3fc.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/e6a5f5644ae4bcdfca4ca26bb258f33378381737ee036142c1e1c24f568ad2ed.png), then what is $AB?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the matrices using the usual method, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i} & \\text{i} \\\\ 1 & 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ \\text{i} & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(-\\text{i})\\cdot (1+2\\text{i})+\\text{i}\\cdot \\text{i} & (-\\text{i})\\cdot (1-\\text{i})+\\text{i}\\cdot 2 \\\\ 1\\cdot (1+2\\text{i})+2\\text{i}\\cdot \\text{i} & 1\\cdot (1-\\text{i})+2\\text{i}\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(2-\\text{i})+(-1) & (-1-\\text{i})+2\\text{i} \\\\ (1+2\\text{i})+(-2) & (1-\\text{i})+4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & -1+\\text{i} \\\\ -1+2\\text{i} & 1+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128910 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7c1b7ad-e4bf-55b2-8665-2cf35e402946" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "e8bc731b-bb0b-5a07-89d9-6acc9beebc82" :question/math-academy-id "e-5903" :question/problem "Find $B=\\overline{A},$ where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/25ce0cd375da320d1615cf49f659ec33e4646cf6bc66455198bec5fd591b3dd3.png) What is the value of $b_{11} + b_{23}?$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}4\\text{i} & 3-\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i} \\\\ 2-2\\text{i} & 2-\\text{i} & 1+2\\text{i} \\\\ \\text{i} & 3\\text{i} & 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{4\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{3-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{1+\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{2-2\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{2-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{1+2\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{3\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{2\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4\\text{i} & 3+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ 2+2\\text{i} & 2+\\text{i} & 1-2\\text{i} \\\\ -\\text{i} & -3\\text{i} & -2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $b_{11} + b_{23} = (-4\\textrm{i}) + (1-2\\textrm{i}) = 1-6\\textrm{i}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368290 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83fad21d-6b36-5198-a13f-362d34342475" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Complex Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac9b3e9f-ae0a-56e9-b155-c3d52e23b595" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}24-20\\text{i} \\\\ 10+51\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368292} {:answer/id #uuid "ce5bac79-1f67-59cf-81ea-7bf6a734fa83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-17-45\\text{i} \\\\ 16-23\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368293} {:answer/id #uuid "1ce53375-edf1-5716-8790-c5a33d9e6fd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}16-23\\text{i} \\\\ -17-45\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368294} {:answer/id #uuid "be709f92-5c51-50a5-8189-d71172f21ac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10+51\\text{i} \\\\ 24-20\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368295} {:answer/id #uuid "a5866125-1746-5c8b-a974-d717c9ac358b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}16-27\\text{i} \\\\ 23-35\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ce53375-edf1-5716-8790-c5a33d9e6fd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}16-23\\text{i} \\\\ -17-45\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368294} :answer-field/id #uuid "354e6696-42a6-58b0-8da2-d63d9ad43936" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368291}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eed0301f-d83a-548c-89d9-f113ce59919b" :question/math-academy-id "q-140329" :question/problem "If $\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}-3+5\\text{i} & 4-3\\text{i} \\\\ -4\\text{i} & 5-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-3\\text{i} \\\\ 4-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$, then $\\,Ax=$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the matrix by the vector using the usual method, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}-3+5\\text{i} & 4-3\\text{i} \\\\ -4\\text{i} & 5-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3\\text{i} \\\\ 4-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(-3+5\\text{i})(-3\\text{i})+(4-3\\text{i})(4-5\\text{i}) \\\\ (-4\\text{i})(-3\\text{i})+(5-5\\text{i})(4-5\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(15+9\\text{i})+(1-32\\text{i}) \\\\ (-12)+(-5-45\\text{i})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16-23\\text{i} \\\\ -17-45\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368297 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2e7753-83f4-5826-a04f-89616d34c578" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations to a Complex Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "973e9ea9-e50c-5c34-a375-c9e1289a6bca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368299} {:answer/id #uuid "0ffb1167-43a6-5c28-8c27-01c63a09de6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\text{i}-3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368300} {:answer/id #uuid "86357dae-ec5f-50c5-b30d-9ce93f504835" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368301} {:answer/id #uuid "3df4d77c-91d8-5371-b762-454aae97e371" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368302} {:answer/id #uuid "3fa79e1f-c9bb-509b-9856-c244502096f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\text{i}-3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3df4d77c-91d8-5371-b762-454aae97e371" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368302} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8046574-c7f6-52c6-b4a5-5f2588341e50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368298}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d85a9a95-fca5-5b64-9704-b7ff3435b87c" :question/math-academy-id "q-140381" :question/problem "Given the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & -2-4\\text{i} \\\\ 3-2\\text{i} & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$, find the result of applying to $A$ the following  elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}=\\frac{1}{1+2\\text{i}}{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}={R}_{2}+(2\\text{i}-3){R}_{1}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the row operations to $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & -2-4\\text{i} \\\\ 3-2\\text{i} & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{1+2\\text{i}}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3-2\\text{i} & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(2\\text{i}-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the result is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 6-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129583 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c28b8ae-71ef-5d26-895a-5d949fc5b164" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Components of the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb6bf39f-fa44-54fb-8394-804a12de1447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127293} {:answer/id #uuid "222e596e-8775-5f76-a4bc-2d52cf201c2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127294} {:answer/id #uuid "3133abda-b21f-50ca-a2a2-b0ca36782460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127295} {:answer/id #uuid "535cd932-d43d-57d7-beee-1e